        <h3 id="werbliche-kommunikation-via-e-mail-post-fax-oder-telefon">Promotional communication via e-mail, post, fax or telephone</h3>
        <p>We process personal data for the purposes of promotional communication, which can be carried out via various channels, such as e-mail, telephone, post or fax, in accordance with legal requirements.</p>
        <p>Recipients have the right to withdraw consents given at any time or to object to promotional communication at any time.</p>
        <p>After withdrawal or objection, we may, on the basis of our legitimate interests, store the data required to prove the consent for up to three years before deleting them. The processing of these data is limited to the purpose of possible defense against claims. An individual deletion request is possible at any time, provided that the former existence of a consent is simultaneously confirmed.</p>
        <p>Types of data processed: Registration data (e.g., names, addresses), contact data (e.g., e-mail, telephone numbers).</p>
        <p>Data subjects: Communication partners.</p>
        <p>Purposes of processing: Direct marketing (e.g., by e-mail or by post).</p>
        <p>Legal bases: Consent (Art. 6 Abs. 1 S. 1 lit. a DSGVO), legitimate interests (Art. 6 Abs. 1 S. 1 lit. f. DSGVO).</p>
        <h3 id="gewinnspiele-und-wettbewerbe">Contests and competitions</h3>
        <p>We process personal data of participants in contests and competitions only in compliance with the applicable data protection provisions, insofar as the processing is contractually necessary for the provision, implementation and settlement of the contest, the participants have consented to the processing, or the processing serves our legitimate interests (e.g., in the security of the contest or in protecting our interests against abuse by, for example, recording IP addresses when contest entries are submitted).</p>
        <p>If participants' entries are published as part of the contests (e.g., as part of a vote or presentation of contest entries or winners or in reporting on the contest), we point out that the names of the participants may also be published in this context. Participants may object to this at any time.</p>
        <p>If the contest takes place within an online platform or a social network (e.g., Facebook or Instagram, hereinafter referred to as "online platform"), the terms of use and privacy policies of the respective platforms also apply. In such cases, we point out that we are responsible for the information provided by the participants in the context of the contest and that enquiries regarding the contest should be addressed to us.</p>
        <p>Participants' data are deleted as soon as the contest or competition has ended and the data are no longer necessary to inform the winners or because follow-up questions regarding the contest are to be expected. As a rule, participants' data are deleted no later than 6 months after the end of the contest. Winners' data may be retained longer in order, for example, to answer queries about the prizes or to fulfill the prizes; in such cases the retention period depends on the nature of the prize and is, for example, up to three years for goods or services in order to be able to process warranty cases. Furthermore, participants' data may be stored for a longer period, e.g., in the form of reporting on the contest in online and offline media.</p>
        <p>If data were also collected for other purposes in connection with the contest, their processing and retention period are governed by the privacy notices for that use (e.g., in the case of signing up for the newsletter as part of a contest).</p>
        <p>Types of data processed: Registration data (e.g., names, addresses), content data (e.g., text entries, photographs, videos).</p>
        <p>Data subjects: Contest and competition participants.</p>
        <p>Purposes of processing: Conducting contests and competitions.</p>
        <p>Legal bases: Performance of a contract and pre-contractual enquiries (Art. 6 Abs. 1 S. 1 lit. b. DSGVO).</p>
        <h3 id="umfragen-und-befragungen">Surveys and questionnaires</h3>
        <p>The surveys and questionnaires conducted by us (hereinafter "surveys") are evaluated anonymously. Personal data are processed only to the extent necessary for the provision and technical execution of the surveys (e.g., processing the IP address in order to display the survey in the user's browser or using a temporary cookie (session cookie) to allow the survey to be resumed) or users have given consent.</p>
        <p>Notes on legal bases: If we ask participants for consent to the processing of their data, this is the legal basis for the processing; otherwise the processing of participants' data is carried out on the basis of our legitimate interests in conducting an objective survey.</p>
        <p>Types of data processed: Contact data (e.g., e-mail, telephone numbers), content data (e.g., text entries, photographs, videos), usage data (e.g., visited websites, interest in content, access times), meta/communication data (e.g., device information, IP addresses).</p>
        <p>Data subjects: Communication partners, users (e.g., website visitors, users of online services).</p>
        <p>Purposes of processing: Contact enquiries and communication, direct marketing (e.g., by e-mail or by post), feedback (e.g., collecting feedback via online form), tracking (e.g., interest-/behavior-based profiling, use of cookies).</p>
        <p>Legal bases: Consent (Art. 6 Abs. 1 S. 1 lit. a DSGVO), legitimate interests (Art. 6 Abs. 1 S. 1 lit. f. DSGVO).</p>
